                    </tr>
                    <tr class="border-b border-border">
                      <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">Cache-Control</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-2">no-store unless the server opted into caching</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                      <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">Content-Language</td>
                      <td class="px-4 py-2">Language an error body was written in</td>
                    </tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Caching -->
        <section id="caching" class="animate-on-scroll">
          <h2 class="mb-4 font-mono text-xl font-semibold text-primary" data-i18n="api.caching">
            Caching
          </h2>
          <p class="mb-4 text-sm text-muted" data-i18n="api.cachingDesc">
            A stored file never changes, so every download carries an ETag and answers 304 Not
            Modified when you send it back in If-None-Match. Whether a browser or CDN may keep the
            response is up to the server operator, via CACHE_MAX_AGE, and it is off by default.
          </p>

          <div class="mb-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-4">
            <pre
              class="font-mono text-xs text-muted"><code>curl -sD - -o /dev/null https://send.to/aB3cD4eF/report.pdf
# ETag: "9f2c…"
# Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, immutable

curl -sD - -o /dev/null -H 'If-None-Match: "9f2c…"' https://send.to/aB3cD4eF/report.pdf
# HTTP/1.1 304 Not Modified</code></pre>
          </div>

          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-muted">
            <li class="flex gap-2">
              <span class="text-accent">-</span>
              <span data-i18n="api.cachingLimited"
                >Files with Max-Downloads are never cacheable — a cached copy is served without the
                origin counting it.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-2">
              <span class="text-accent">-</span>
              <span data-i18n="api.cachingEncrypted"
                >Server-side encrypted files are never cacheable — they are decrypted per request
                against a password header.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-2">
              <span class="text-accent">-</span>
              <span data-i18n="api.cachingDelete"
                >When caching is on, a deleted file stays reachable through the cache until its
                max-age runs out.</span
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- Languages -->
        <section id="languages" class="animate-on-scroll">
          <h2 class="mb-4 font-mono text-xl font-semibold text-primary" data-i18n="api.languages">
            Languages
          </h2>
          <p class="mb-4 text-sm text-muted" data-i18n="api.languagesDesc">
            Error messages follow Accept-Language, in English, Chinese and Japanese. A request
            without the header gets English, and the response says which language it used in
            Content-Language.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-surface p-4">
            <pre
              class="font-mono text-xs text-muted"><code>curl -H 'Accept-Language: zh-CN' https://send.to/nosuchtoken/x.bin
# 未找到</code></pre>
          </div>
        </section>

